1
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:54,179
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

2
00:01:33,426 --> 00:01:35,970
Wait. We're not done talking.

3
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:44,646
What?

4
00:02:12,549 --> 00:02:14,342
Father, stay inside!

5
00:02:34,696 --> 00:02:35,738
It's from the bathroom.

6
00:02:36,823 --> 00:02:37,907
Stay back.

7
00:02:45,623 --> 00:02:47,000
You, get out of the way!

8
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:20,617
It's not me.

9
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:22,994
Move!

10
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,450
Hands in the air.

11
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:16,839
Hands up!

12
00:04:30,645 --> 00:04:31,938
Open it now!

13
00:04:32,021 --> 00:04:33,273
Break the door!

14
00:04:34,148 --> 00:04:35,233
Open it already!

15
00:04:48,579 --> 00:04:50,623
Father, stay there!

16
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:08,975
Make one wrong move, and I'll shoot.

17
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:56,773
Get him! He's the killer!

18
00:06:38,189 --> 00:06:40,316
So-ran, are you okay?

19
00:07:07,885 --> 00:07:08,928
Mr. Suzuki.

20
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:12,473
Mr. Suzuki?

21
00:07:15,059 --> 00:07:15,977
Mr. Suzuki.

22
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:19,605
Father! Are you all right?

23
00:07:58,269 --> 00:08:03,399
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

24
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:05,776
EPISODE 2

25
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:47,777
Are you one of them?

26
00:08:48,819 --> 00:08:50,863
Where did he run off to? Say it!

27
00:08:52,573 --> 00:08:54,784
I had nothing to do with it, I swear!

28
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:04,544
But first, I have something to tell you.

29
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:11,050
Honey.

30
00:09:15,471 --> 00:09:16,305
Honey?

31
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:18,599
What is it?

32
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:21,227
Are you going to prove
that you're not involved?

33
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:23,646
Yes, I can prove it.

34
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:27,483
That maid isn't one of them.

35
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:39,704
When the killer brought her
to the bathroom as a hostage,

36
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:41,747
she warned me of an assassination.

37
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:44,250
Thanks to her, I could act quickly.

38
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:48,170
In other words, it was her

39
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:49,964
who saved me and my father.

40
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:51,632
By the way, Chief.

41
00:09:52,842 --> 00:09:55,177
How did he even get past security?

42
00:09:59,765 --> 00:10:00,641
Take her.

43
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:03,102
I have something to tell you…

44
00:10:03,185 --> 00:10:04,604
I have something to tell you!

45
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:07,023
Honey.

46
00:10:07,773 --> 00:10:08,608
Honey.

47
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:12,236
We need to lay her down now.

48
00:10:13,988 --> 00:10:15,448
Help me, Seo-hee.

49
00:10:16,991 --> 00:10:18,784
Keum Seo-hee!

50
00:10:28,586 --> 00:10:29,420
Yes, ma'am!

51
00:10:29,503 --> 00:10:30,421
Freeze!

52
00:10:38,554 --> 00:10:40,514
Are you going
to take responsibility for this?

53
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:47,647
If anything happens
to my wife and my baby…

54
00:10:52,234 --> 00:10:57,406
I'll hold the Government-General
accountable through the U.S. Consulate.

55
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:14,298
Let her go.

56
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:39,240
Think carefully.

57
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:42,368
Saying useless things now
isn't going to help you.

58
00:11:42,451 --> 00:11:44,829
If you want your 60 won,
you'd better cooperate.

59
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:47,915
I know.

60
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:50,084
That's why I'm here.

61
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:53,671
But…

62
00:11:54,505 --> 00:11:56,298
I think you owe me 100 won.

63
00:11:56,382 --> 00:11:57,883
I nearly got killed too.

64
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:09,562
Put the guns down!

65
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:15,067
Why were you hiding a gun?

66
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:19,780
With things so dangerous these days,
it's for self-defense.

67
00:12:21,741 --> 00:12:23,033
I already had it on me

68
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:26,454
when the police searched me before dinner.

69
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:31,459
Mr. Yoo Philip fired the gun
at the killer,

70
00:12:32,543 --> 00:12:33,377
but he missed.

71
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:37,131
If you keep suspecting us,

72
00:12:37,214 --> 00:12:40,384
I'll have no choice but to write
about what happened tonight.

73
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:46,557
Someone tried to assassinate
the new inspector general.

74
00:12:47,183 --> 00:12:51,187
Could the killer be someone
opposed to Japan's rule of Joseon?

75
00:12:51,937 --> 00:12:53,314
If news like this gets out,

76
00:12:53,397 --> 00:12:55,483
what will the world think of Japan?

77
00:12:55,566 --> 00:12:56,984
The international community

78
00:12:57,067 --> 00:12:59,779
is already watching Japan
because of Manchukuo.

79
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:07,203
I can personally vouch
for our maid's identity.

80
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:10,331
Don't lay a hand on her again

81
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:12,124
and stop suspecting her.

82
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:17,171
Consider this a warning.

83
00:13:18,798 --> 00:13:19,673
Chief!

84
00:13:21,717 --> 00:13:22,802
Did you find him?

85
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:23,719
Yes, sir.

86
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:28,516
He's the cake deliveryman from Itsukoshi.

87
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:30,476
He was knocked out on a delivery.

88
00:13:30,559 --> 00:13:33,479
When he woke up,
his uniform and bike were gone.

89
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:35,147
Are you sure?

90
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:37,775
I swear it's true. I'm not lying!

91
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:02,341
I hope your wife feels better soon.

92
00:15:00,107 --> 00:15:02,610
Do you have any idea what you've done?

93
00:15:04,486 --> 00:15:05,571
I have…

94
00:15:07,031 --> 00:15:09,783
waited so long for this day.

95
00:15:09,867 --> 00:15:11,035
You just…

96
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:14,747
destroyed everything I've ever lived for!

97
00:15:17,291 --> 00:15:18,125
Well…

98
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:20,377
I mean…

99
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:24,048
This wouldn't have happened
if you'd just paid me earlier.

100
00:15:24,131 --> 00:15:26,342
Money?

101
00:15:27,259 --> 00:15:30,763
You ruined everything over a little money.
Are you happy now?

102
00:15:30,846 --> 00:15:34,600
Do you even realize what you've done
for that stupid money?

103
00:15:35,309 --> 00:15:37,227
Don't blame me.

104
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:38,938
I nearly died myself.

105
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:46,320
Just give me the money you promised.

106
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:53,869
Bring me the bullets first.

107
00:15:58,248 --> 00:16:00,167
Seriously, I knew it.

108
00:16:02,586 --> 00:16:04,755
Forget it. I'll just sell them myself.

109
00:16:04,838 --> 00:16:06,590
Seriously, though,

110
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:08,842
I would have brought you the bullets
if you'd paid me.

111
00:16:09,426 --> 00:16:12,471
But whatever. It's no big deal.
I can do without it.

112
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:14,181
It's no big deal?

113
00:16:14,264 --> 00:16:17,643
Yeah. I never imagined I'd get involved
in the independence movement

114
00:16:17,726 --> 00:16:19,812
and nearly die over a little money.

115
00:16:20,729 --> 00:16:22,272
So forget the money.

116
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:25,442
Good luck with the independence movement.
Don't fail next time.

117
00:16:25,526 --> 00:16:27,361
Don't you care about your own country?

118
00:16:29,321 --> 00:16:31,573
Why does everyone
keep saying the same thing?

119
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:33,867
Look.

120
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:37,246
I was born into a country
already under Japanese rule.

121
00:16:37,329 --> 00:16:38,831
Is that my fault?

122
00:16:38,914 --> 00:16:40,916
You can't blame me, can you?

123
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,544
Am I supposed to fight for independence
just because I was born in Joseon?

124
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:47,589
What has Joseon ever done for me?

125
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,431
You want to fire a gun here?

126
00:16:56,557 --> 00:16:58,267
The police are still outside.

127
00:17:00,853 --> 00:17:02,813
I'm not a snitch.

128
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:05,941
I already told them
I'm the live-in maid here.

129
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:08,027
If you get caught,
do you think I'll be safe?

130
00:17:11,947 --> 00:17:14,825
There's no way we'll see each other again.

131
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:16,785
Believe me, I deeply regret

132
00:17:17,661 --> 00:17:19,538
ever setting foot in this house.

133
00:17:24,793 --> 00:17:25,919
Let her go.

134
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:29,131
So-ran.

135
00:17:29,214 --> 00:17:31,884
Today's operation
has already fallen through.

136
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:32,801
Still, if--

137
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:35,220
Besides, she has a point.

138
00:17:44,855 --> 00:17:47,441
If you stole anything,
give it back before you go.

139
00:17:47,524 --> 00:17:48,734
Stole something?

140
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:51,153
What are you talking about?

141
00:17:51,236 --> 00:17:52,654
Should I search you?

142
00:18:05,292 --> 00:18:06,126
Happy now?

143
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:09,505
I was going to switch the photo
and go to America.

144
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:10,422
America?

145
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:13,675
Yes, I'm saving up so I can go to America.

146
00:18:14,802 --> 00:18:16,011
You can't go there.

147
00:18:17,054 --> 00:18:18,972
They won't take you in.

148
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:20,891
What?

149
00:18:20,974 --> 00:18:22,851
I said you can't go to America.

150
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:26,021
If you don't believe me,
ask the U.S. Consulate.

151
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:28,315
Do you realize you're being so childish?

152
00:18:42,204 --> 00:18:43,705
So-ran, are you okay?

153
00:18:44,331 --> 00:18:45,499
Are you hurt anywhere?

154
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:48,043
No, I'm fine.

155
00:18:50,587 --> 00:18:53,715
Thanks to you shooting him,
we're in the clear for now.

156
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:58,929
I think he's an independence fighter,
but I have no idea where he came from.

157
00:18:59,012 --> 00:19:01,390
The Provisional Government
knows we're trying to kill Sato,

158
00:19:01,473 --> 00:19:02,850
so I doubt he's with them.

159
00:19:08,313 --> 00:19:10,190
His name is Keum Seok-jung.

160
00:19:14,611 --> 00:19:15,529
Do you know him?

161
00:19:18,031 --> 00:19:20,868
For 13 years,
I didn't know if he was alive or dead.

162
00:19:23,912 --> 00:19:27,499
<i>I wanted nothing more than</i>
<i>to find him and kill him.</i>

163
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:35,674
He's my husband.

164
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:11,293
You.

165
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,921
Are you really the maid here?

166
00:20:14,796 --> 00:20:16,798
Enough with the lies. Tell me the truth.

167
00:20:17,382 --> 00:20:19,134
Who are you really, Keum Seo-hee?

168
00:20:19,843 --> 00:20:22,304
I am the live-in maid here.
You heard that earlier.

169
00:20:22,387 --> 00:20:23,764
Stop lying.

170
00:20:23,847 --> 00:20:26,141
If that's true,
why were you in first class?

171
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:27,434
And what about today?

172
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:30,771
I've never heard of a live-in maid
who speaks English.

173
00:20:30,854 --> 00:20:32,564
I'll take that as a compliment.

174
00:20:32,648 --> 00:20:34,942
I couldn't go to school,
so I couldn't get any other job.

175
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:36,652
But that's not my fault, is it?

176
00:20:37,152 --> 00:20:39,529
If you're really the live-in maid here,

177
00:20:39,613 --> 00:20:41,490
what are you doing outside now?

178
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:42,616
The house is a mess.

179
00:20:42,699 --> 00:20:44,868
You should be cleaning
or tending to the madam.

180
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:47,829
I'm out getting medicine for her.

181
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:49,289
As you know,

182
00:20:49,373 --> 00:20:51,917
she's not feeling great
after what happened earlier.

183
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,419
So would you mind letting me through?
I need to go.

184
00:20:54,503 --> 00:20:55,963
If you keep suspecting me,

185
00:20:56,046 --> 00:20:57,881
I'll tell the inspector general.

186
00:20:57,965 --> 00:20:59,424
I did save his life earlier--

187
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:01,134
You're going to see my father?

188
00:21:02,594 --> 00:21:03,679
Your father?

189
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:07,015
Father, stay inside!

190
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:12,104
Yes, your father.
Let's go talk to him together.

191
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:15,190
Let's tell him
you're treating me like I'm a pickpocket.

192
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:18,151
He seemed like a fair and reasonable man.
Then surely…

193
00:21:20,487 --> 00:21:21,905
What do you even know?

194
00:21:23,031 --> 00:21:23,865
Excuse me?

195
00:21:37,629 --> 00:21:40,173
This is a waste of time.
Let's stop arguing.

196
00:21:40,257 --> 00:21:43,176
I won't ask who you really are anymore.

197
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,594
Just give me back what's in my wallet.

198
00:21:45,971 --> 00:21:47,639
You can keep the wallet and the money.

199
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:49,099
I'll let this all go.

200
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:51,601
What's in the wallet?

201
00:21:55,022 --> 00:21:55,939
Not worth a thing.

202
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:00,819
Look.

203
00:22:01,611 --> 00:22:04,281
You keep going on about your wallet,

204
00:22:04,364 --> 00:22:07,409
but I honestly have no idea
what you're talking about.

205
00:22:08,952 --> 00:22:10,912
This is rather strange.

206
00:22:10,996 --> 00:22:14,458
If you're so sure I stole your wallet,

207
00:22:14,541 --> 00:22:17,210
why not take me to the police?

208
00:22:20,589 --> 00:22:24,426
I suppose you don't want anyone
finding out what's in your wallet.

209
00:22:24,509 --> 00:22:27,721
Whatever it is, it's useless to you.

210
00:22:28,472 --> 00:22:30,599
I'll let you keep the wallet and money.

211
00:22:30,682 --> 00:22:32,184
Why do you keep denying you have it?

212
00:22:32,267 --> 00:22:34,102
I'm not denying anything.

213
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:36,063
I really don't know.

214
00:22:40,692 --> 00:22:44,237
If I hadn't helped you earlier,
you'd have been taken for an accomplice.

215
00:22:46,490 --> 00:22:48,450
Yet you don't seem grateful at all.

216
00:22:48,533 --> 00:22:51,036
You could say the same about yourself.

217
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:53,455
You would've died
if it weren't for me, right?

218
00:22:53,538 --> 00:22:55,707
Yet here you are,
calling your lifesaver a thief--

219
00:22:55,791 --> 00:22:56,917
Excuse me.

220
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,043
Seo-hee!

221
00:22:59,586 --> 00:23:00,545
Seo-hee!

222
00:23:01,713 --> 00:23:02,547
Yes, sir!

223
00:23:02,631 --> 00:23:04,257
What are you doing there?

224
00:23:04,341 --> 00:23:05,175
Come on.

225
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:11,681
Yes, I'm coming.

226
00:23:16,937 --> 00:23:18,230
- Let's go.
- Okay.

227
00:23:40,836 --> 00:23:42,254
I didn't know you were here, Hideo.

228
00:23:43,213 --> 00:23:44,464
Are you going somewhere?

229
00:23:44,548 --> 00:23:47,676
Yes, my wife's not feeling well,
so I called a cab.

230
00:23:47,759 --> 00:23:49,219
Excuse me, but I have to run.

231
00:23:53,014 --> 00:23:55,016
Go to the Imperial University
Affiliated Clinic.

232
00:24:19,124 --> 00:24:21,710
I saw you with Sato Hideo outside,
so I called you over.

233
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:23,253
What were you talking about with him?

234
00:24:23,879 --> 00:24:24,880
Sato Hi…

235
00:24:27,007 --> 00:24:28,091
Sato Hideo?

236
00:24:28,633 --> 00:24:29,551
Well…

237
00:25:39,329 --> 00:25:40,330
You can't come in.

238
00:25:42,249 --> 00:25:43,625
Please wait outside.

239
00:25:47,629 --> 00:25:49,256
When did the bleeding start?

240
00:25:50,799 --> 00:25:53,093
Dr. Kim, I've got her.

241
00:25:53,176 --> 00:25:55,929
I'll call if I need you.
Go help with the gunshot patient.

242
00:25:56,012 --> 00:25:56,888
Okay.

243
00:26:01,977 --> 00:26:03,520
What happened?

244
00:26:03,603 --> 00:26:05,355
Suzuki was brought in
with a gunshot wound.

245
00:26:05,438 --> 00:26:06,481
He's in surgery now.

246
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:09,234
We failed.

247
00:26:10,819 --> 00:26:13,822
There was someone else
with the same goal as us.

248
00:26:14,364 --> 00:26:17,033
He shot at Sato before I could.

249
00:26:17,784 --> 00:26:20,870
He fled after getting into a shootout
with Sato's son.

250
00:26:23,123 --> 00:26:25,500
For now, we're in the clear,

251
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:27,502
but not entirely.

252
00:26:27,586 --> 00:26:29,879
So let's say I miscarried
because of the shooting.

253
00:26:30,463 --> 00:26:31,423
We told Sato's son

254
00:26:31,506 --> 00:26:33,466
we'd rushed here.

255
00:26:34,009 --> 00:26:36,303
Sato will probably want to check tomorrow.

256
00:26:36,886 --> 00:26:38,054
Understood.

257
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:41,850
Did you get shot?

258
00:26:41,933 --> 00:26:43,226
No.

259
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:45,520
I figured people would notice me
coming and going,

260
00:26:45,604 --> 00:26:47,230
so I gave myself a little cut.

261
00:26:47,314 --> 00:26:48,231
Let me take a look.

262
00:26:50,275 --> 00:26:51,776
I'll clean the wound. Bear with me.

263
00:26:56,031 --> 00:26:58,408
Who's the woman you came with?

264
00:27:08,585 --> 00:27:09,461
Well…

265
00:27:10,337 --> 00:27:11,921
She'll be all right, won't she?

266
00:27:26,186 --> 00:27:28,521
We couldn't save the baby.

267
00:27:29,731 --> 00:27:30,649
I'm sorry.

268
00:27:31,483 --> 00:27:34,986
She'll recover after some rest.

269
00:28:07,018 --> 00:28:09,437
Yes, Your Excellency, Governor-General!

270
00:28:12,649 --> 00:28:13,817
Yes, sir.

271
00:28:13,900 --> 00:28:15,610
The American reporter is unharmed.

272
00:28:15,694 --> 00:28:17,779
<i>Didn't I make it clear already?</i>

273
00:28:17,862 --> 00:28:19,739
<i>We must not let the American reporter</i>

274
00:28:19,823 --> 00:28:22,450
<i>detect even a hint of unrest in Joseon.</i>

275
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:24,494
<i>Our priority at the Government-General</i>

276
00:28:24,577 --> 00:28:27,539
<i>is getting</i>
<i>the League of Nations Commission</i>

277
00:28:27,622 --> 00:28:34,504
<i>currently in China to recognize Manchukuo</i>
<i>as a legitimate independent state.</i>

278
00:28:34,587 --> 00:28:38,591
<i>We must show the world</i>
<i>that Manchukuo can become</i>

279
00:28:38,675 --> 00:28:42,512
<i>as peaceful as Joseon under Japanese rule.</i>

280
00:28:42,595 --> 00:28:43,930
<i>Is that clear?</i>

281
00:28:44,013 --> 00:28:45,348
Yes, sir!

282
00:28:59,404 --> 00:29:00,238
Father.

283
00:29:01,948 --> 00:29:05,618
Mr. Yoo's wife was rushed
to the hospital with bleeding.

284
00:29:19,132 --> 00:29:21,968
She's quite ill,
so please keep a close eye on her.

285
00:29:22,051 --> 00:29:23,887
Let me know right away
if anything happens.

286
00:29:24,804 --> 00:29:26,806
I'm putting together your 100 won.

287
00:29:27,557 --> 00:29:29,601
Stay here tonight. I'll pay you tomorrow.

288
00:29:31,227 --> 00:29:32,061
Okay.

289
00:29:35,315 --> 00:29:36,399
Let me help you.

290
00:29:36,483 --> 00:29:38,151
No, it's okay.

291
00:29:39,819 --> 00:29:42,155
Honey, help me get changed.

292
00:29:43,823 --> 00:29:44,657
Careful.

293
00:31:17,917 --> 00:31:20,587
Are you sure
you weren't hurt anywhere else?

294
00:31:21,421 --> 00:31:22,630
Yeah, I'm fine.

295
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:24,966
This is just a little graze.

296
00:31:26,968 --> 00:31:27,927
All done.

297
00:31:31,764 --> 00:31:32,849
Thank you.

298
00:31:34,976 --> 00:31:36,936
It's late. You should go to bed.

299
00:31:37,020 --> 00:31:39,606
It's way past your bedtime.

300
00:31:39,689 --> 00:31:42,317
No, I don't want to go to bed.

301
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:43,568
Don't push me.

302
00:31:43,651 --> 00:31:45,403
I said don't push me.

303
00:31:45,486 --> 00:31:46,654
Good night.

304
00:31:47,572 --> 00:31:48,448
Good night.

305
00:31:48,531 --> 00:31:49,908
I hate you, Ms. Yanagi.

306
00:31:49,991 --> 00:31:51,492
You're the worst!

307
00:31:51,576 --> 00:31:53,578
I hate you.

308
00:31:54,162 --> 00:31:55,371
Good night, Hanako.

309
00:31:55,455 --> 00:31:56,873
Hideo!

310
00:32:10,637 --> 00:32:12,221
Father! Are you all right?

311
00:32:15,558 --> 00:32:17,685
Father!

312
00:32:18,353 --> 00:32:20,271
Mother's gone. Mother…

313
00:32:22,607 --> 00:32:23,775
Father…

314
00:32:25,568 --> 00:32:26,861
It's me.

315
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:30,657
Hideo.

316
00:32:35,620 --> 00:32:36,996
What is it?

317
00:32:38,790 --> 00:32:39,874
Mother…

318
00:32:41,209 --> 00:32:42,627
She left home.

319
00:32:44,128 --> 00:32:45,338
Is…

320
00:32:45,922 --> 00:32:48,758
Is that true, Father?

321
00:34:19,891 --> 00:34:20,933
Are you up?

322
00:34:35,490 --> 00:34:38,201
Still haven't caught him yet?
Are you serious right now?

323
00:34:39,118 --> 00:34:41,496
We're drawing up a sketch now.

324
00:34:46,209 --> 00:34:47,752
Get going now.

325
00:34:49,212 --> 00:34:50,213
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir.

326
00:34:51,255 --> 00:34:52,173
And you.

327
00:34:54,383 --> 00:34:55,885
Who did you say showed up in Keijo?

328
00:34:55,968 --> 00:34:59,680
Han Cheol-yong,
a key member of the Gugukdan.

329
00:34:59,764 --> 00:35:00,932
Han Cheol-yong?

330
00:35:02,475 --> 00:35:03,351
Is that confirmed?

331
00:35:04,560 --> 00:35:05,561
Yes, sir.

332
00:35:05,645 --> 00:35:08,981
He was behind the attempted assassination
of the Jongno police chief 12 years ago.

333
00:35:09,065 --> 00:35:11,692
He was released two years ago
and went to Shanghai.

334
00:35:11,776 --> 00:35:14,654
Then he was spotted in Jongno
three days ago.

335
00:35:14,737 --> 00:35:17,990
The police inspector
who'd interrogated him before saw him.

336
00:35:19,575 --> 00:35:21,202
Bring me his surveillance card.

337
00:35:29,043 --> 00:35:31,295
NAME
HAN CHEOL-YONG

338
00:35:34,006 --> 00:35:35,716
Gugukdan, is it?

339
00:35:38,678 --> 00:35:40,263
Were you with the Gugukdan?

340
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:44,976
How long did you think you could hide it?

341
00:35:48,521 --> 00:35:49,647
Gugukdan.

342
00:35:51,065 --> 00:35:52,817
I haven't heard that name in a while.

343
00:35:54,402 --> 00:35:56,863
Could this be some kind of fate?

344
00:35:57,446 --> 00:35:58,614
Sorry?

345
00:35:59,198 --> 00:36:03,327
I'll report to the governor-general that
the Gugukdan was behind the attack.

346
00:36:03,411 --> 00:36:06,873
But that's still just speculation.

347
00:36:06,956 --> 00:36:10,585
We won't know for sure if it really was
the Gugukdan until we arrest him.

348
00:36:10,668 --> 00:36:14,088
It doesn't matter anymore
who they really were yesterday.

349
00:36:14,839 --> 00:36:16,966
We'll just pin it on the Gugukdan.

350
00:36:17,758 --> 00:36:19,969
They've been a thorn in our side
for years.

351
00:36:20,052 --> 00:36:22,430
We'll use this chance to wipe them out.

352
00:36:24,140 --> 00:36:25,183
Is that clear?

353
00:36:25,892 --> 00:36:26,726
Yes, sir!

354
00:36:42,992 --> 00:36:44,202
Come in.

355
00:36:55,421 --> 00:36:56,964
She's not coming back.

356
00:36:57,632 --> 00:36:59,634
She was with Sato Hideo last night.

357
00:36:59,717 --> 00:37:01,302
That doesn't sit right with me.

358
00:37:01,385 --> 00:37:03,304
Could she have gone to him to betray us--

359
00:37:08,309 --> 00:37:09,977
The streetcar took forever to come.

360
00:37:16,150 --> 00:37:16,984
Here.

361
00:37:20,196 --> 00:37:24,617
I brought you some seaweed
and a little beef.

362
00:37:26,744 --> 00:37:28,454
I hope you get well.

363
00:37:44,303 --> 00:37:45,513
Here's the 100 won I promised.

364
00:37:51,060 --> 00:37:52,603
Open it and check the amount.

365
00:37:54,814 --> 00:37:58,067
It's fine. You wouldn't shortchange
someone who nearly died.

366
00:37:58,734 --> 00:38:00,820
All right. Then let's part ways here.

367
00:38:01,487 --> 00:38:04,323
We'll say you quit
because you were scared off by last night.

368
00:38:04,907 --> 00:38:07,368
Fine. I'll be going then.

369
00:38:16,502 --> 00:38:17,837
Actually, no.

370
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:20,339
I'll just take
enough for the beef and seaweed.

371
00:38:29,223 --> 00:38:31,434
I don't think
we should see each other again.

372
00:38:31,517 --> 00:38:35,563
So I won't give back what's in your bag.

373
00:38:35,646 --> 00:38:36,689
Fine.

374
00:38:37,523 --> 00:38:38,816
Let's not see each other again.

375
00:38:55,207 --> 00:38:57,543
I don't think
we should let her go like this.

376
00:38:58,169 --> 00:39:00,546
She seems to be quite loyal.
It should be fine.

377
00:39:00,629 --> 00:39:04,175
Our mission fell apart
because of her greed for money.

378
00:39:04,258 --> 00:39:05,968
So we should tell our comrades--

379
00:39:06,052 --> 00:39:07,428
Do you want to get rid of her?

380
00:39:10,598 --> 00:39:12,058
That's not like you,

381
00:39:12,141 --> 00:39:13,934
to think about hurting someone.

382
00:39:14,018 --> 00:39:18,147
Your safety matters more to me than
anything, more than anyone else's life.

383
00:39:27,323 --> 00:39:28,657
I just hope…

384
00:39:30,534 --> 00:39:32,620
you never have to kill anyone.

385
00:39:33,412 --> 00:39:34,497
No matter who they are.

386
00:39:34,580 --> 00:39:36,832
Even if it's for independence,

387
00:39:37,333 --> 00:39:39,001
I don't want you to ever do that.

388
00:39:42,963 --> 00:39:45,341
I've always wanted to tell you this.

389
00:39:46,842 --> 00:39:50,596
And since I survived,
I finally have the chance.

390
00:39:50,679 --> 00:39:51,639
Please, promise me.

391
00:39:54,225 --> 00:39:55,976
Don't pick up a gun.

392
00:40:05,945 --> 00:40:09,156
We promised in Shanghai.

393
00:40:10,699 --> 00:40:11,909
Leave the guns to me.

394
00:40:12,576 --> 00:40:13,994
That's our job.

395
00:40:14,829 --> 00:40:17,164
You use your pen and your words.

396
00:40:17,957 --> 00:40:21,877
Tell the world how Japan stole Joseon's
sovereignty and committed atrocities.

397
00:40:24,255 --> 00:40:26,340
We'll handle the guns and bombs.

398
00:40:28,008 --> 00:40:29,009
As for you,

399
00:40:29,677 --> 00:40:32,930
once we kill Sato,
let the world know what happened.

400
00:40:37,601 --> 00:40:39,061
Even though I'm your husband,

401
00:40:39,145 --> 00:40:41,814
I'm still not part of the "us"
you're talking about.

402
00:40:52,241 --> 00:40:54,994
Even if she comes back asking for money,

403
00:40:55,786 --> 00:40:59,081
I'll have already killed Sato
and be gone by then.

404
00:41:14,263 --> 00:41:15,347
Where did it go?

405
00:41:16,682 --> 00:41:17,975
I know I tossed it here.

406
00:41:21,687 --> 00:41:25,191
Kkot-nim, you barely ate. Why are you
going to the outhouse so often?

407
00:41:25,858 --> 00:41:27,860
Because my tummy hurts.

408
00:41:27,943 --> 00:41:28,819
Hey, No-ma!

409
00:41:28,903 --> 00:41:30,237
You scared me.

410
00:41:30,321 --> 00:41:31,697
- Ga-kyung.
- Hey.

411
00:41:31,780 --> 00:41:34,408
Did you see that here?

412
00:41:34,492 --> 00:41:35,534
That…

413
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:37,912
That? What's that?

414
00:41:37,995 --> 00:41:39,788
Hey, why'd you bring the tissue box?

415
00:41:39,872 --> 00:41:41,957
What was it called? That…

416
00:41:42,958 --> 00:41:45,461
Right, Lee Ga-kyung.
Where'd you sleep last night?

417
00:41:45,544 --> 00:41:46,879
We were worried all night.

418
00:41:46,962 --> 00:41:50,925
We thought you'd gone to America
without telling us.

419
00:41:51,509 --> 00:41:52,384
No.

420
00:41:52,468 --> 00:41:54,553
I can't afford to go to America yet.

421
00:41:54,637 --> 00:41:57,014
That's not important. Did you…

422
00:41:57,097 --> 00:41:58,390
not see a piece of paper?

423
00:41:58,974 --> 00:42:00,184
What paper?

424
00:42:00,267 --> 00:42:02,353
That… pawn ticket!

425
00:42:02,436 --> 00:42:04,688
You know, the pawn ticket I found
in the wallet I stole.

426
00:42:04,772 --> 00:42:05,981
I threw it in here.

427
00:42:06,065 --> 00:42:08,067
But I can't find it. Where did it go?

428
00:42:11,570 --> 00:42:14,448
Where are you coming back from?

429
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:15,991
The outhouse.

430
00:42:16,075 --> 00:42:18,035
Kkot-nim finally had to go
after five days.

431
00:42:18,118 --> 00:42:18,953
What?

432
00:42:20,704 --> 00:42:21,664
Kkot-nim.

433
00:42:22,623 --> 00:42:26,001
Did you take the paper from here?

434
00:42:26,502 --> 00:42:28,546
You didn't, right? Please say you didn't.

435
00:42:31,173 --> 00:42:33,092
If not here, where else would she get it?

436
00:42:36,053 --> 00:42:37,429
Oh, no!

437
00:42:37,930 --> 00:42:40,015
That's what my life depends on.

438
00:42:40,099 --> 00:42:40,975
Your life?

439
00:42:41,058 --> 00:42:42,726
Hey, what are you talking about?

440
00:42:42,810 --> 00:42:44,812
Hey, you're constipated.

441
00:42:44,895 --> 00:42:47,022
Of all days, why today?

442
00:42:47,815 --> 00:42:49,149
What am I supposed to do?

443
00:42:51,735 --> 00:42:53,195
I've got to do something.

444
00:42:54,405 --> 00:42:55,906
I have to get it out. Hold on.

445
00:42:55,990 --> 00:42:58,075
Ga-kyung, the thing is…

446
00:42:58,158 --> 00:42:59,702
Not now. I'm busy.

447
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:02,663
I didn't poop today.

448
00:43:07,376 --> 00:43:08,252
Give me that.

449
00:43:15,509 --> 00:43:16,510
Thank goodness.

450
00:43:20,931 --> 00:43:22,224
Good girl, Kkot-nim.

451
00:43:25,436 --> 00:43:27,313
"Sin Tae-jin."

452
00:43:27,938 --> 00:43:30,399
"1919."

453
00:43:30,482 --> 00:43:31,358
SIN TAE-JIN

454
00:43:31,442 --> 00:43:35,070
Who's Sin Tae-jin?
What did he leave at the pawnshop?

455
00:43:36,780 --> 00:43:38,324
Is it that important?

456
00:43:42,703 --> 00:43:43,537
No way.

457
00:43:43,621 --> 00:43:44,872
I'm never giving it back.

458
00:43:44,955 --> 00:43:48,292
This is my lifeline until I go to America.

459
00:43:57,718 --> 00:43:59,219
ONE WON

460
00:44:01,305 --> 00:44:04,933
I nearly died because of those people.

461
00:44:05,017 --> 00:44:07,102
Maybe I should've taken
the entire 100 won.

462
00:44:08,103 --> 00:44:10,856
I've waited so long for this day.

463
00:44:10,939 --> 00:44:12,066
You just…

464
00:44:12,650 --> 00:44:15,653
destroyed everything I've ever lived for!

465
00:44:19,615 --> 00:44:20,866
Forget it.

466
00:44:20,949 --> 00:44:23,744
Why get mixed up
with dangerous people over 100 won?

467
00:44:23,827 --> 00:44:25,162
It does me no good.

468
00:44:25,996 --> 00:44:27,831
I absolutely cannot die.

469
00:44:28,582 --> 00:44:32,711
I'm going to survive
and make it to America.

470
00:44:36,090 --> 00:44:38,926
Interpreter Suzuki has been placed
on sick leave.

471
00:44:39,009 --> 00:44:43,013
But we can't leave the interpreter's post
vacant for long.

472
00:44:44,181 --> 00:44:45,224
For the time being,

473
00:44:45,307 --> 00:44:47,726
you'll serve
as a temporary English interpreter.

474
00:44:47,810 --> 00:44:49,353
Yes, sir.

475
00:44:49,436 --> 00:44:50,688
Because of Manchukuo,

476
00:44:50,771 --> 00:44:53,482
we need to manage the foreign press now
more than ever.

477
00:44:54,400 --> 00:44:56,193
As an English interpreter,

478
00:44:56,276 --> 00:44:58,946
make sure to manage
the Western journalists well.

479
00:45:00,114 --> 00:45:02,449
Both Tokyo
and His Excellency the governor-general

480
00:45:02,533 --> 00:45:04,034
have their eyes on it.

481
00:45:05,119 --> 00:45:05,953
Yes, sir.

482
00:45:06,036 --> 00:45:08,872
Pay particular attention to Yoo Philip.

483
00:45:09,915 --> 00:45:11,834
I heard his wife
was discharged this morning.

484
00:45:11,917 --> 00:45:14,086
Go in my stead
and offer her my sympathies.

485
00:45:14,628 --> 00:45:17,005
He's American, but he's of Joseon descent,

486
00:45:17,589 --> 00:45:20,759
so I've been keeping a close eye on him.

487
00:45:21,385 --> 00:45:22,720
Then yesterday happened.

488
00:45:23,762 --> 00:45:25,723
Even if he did shoot the killer,

489
00:45:25,806 --> 00:45:27,182
don't let your guard down.

490
00:45:27,766 --> 00:45:30,144
The fact that he had a gun feels off.

491
00:45:31,145 --> 00:45:32,187
I…

492
00:45:33,147 --> 00:45:35,399
I don't trust <i>Josenjing</i>.

493
00:45:43,782 --> 00:45:44,825
Do you trust me?

494
00:45:49,872 --> 00:45:52,082
You're my son, Sato Hideo.

495
00:45:53,542 --> 00:45:55,794
Then why did you point a gun at me?

496
00:46:01,925 --> 00:46:03,719
The day Mother left us…

497
00:46:07,222 --> 00:46:09,266
you pointed a gun at me.

498
00:46:11,518 --> 00:46:12,478
Why on earth…

499
00:46:16,106 --> 00:46:18,275
I wondered why, but I never asked.

500
00:46:18,901 --> 00:46:21,445
Instead, I tried to be a son
you could be proud of.

501
00:46:23,572 --> 00:46:25,407
I tried desperately to prove myself.

502
00:46:27,326 --> 00:46:29,369
I was afraid you'd abandon me too.

503
00:46:32,539 --> 00:46:33,665
I was afraid…

504
00:46:34,541 --> 00:46:36,418
I'd be left alone again.

505
00:46:41,089 --> 00:46:43,884
And yet you pointed a gun at me again.

506
00:46:44,968 --> 00:46:46,762
Now I want to know why.

507
00:46:50,390 --> 00:46:51,767
What do I have to do…

508
00:46:53,811 --> 00:46:55,813
to be your son?

509
00:46:57,064 --> 00:46:57,981
Tell me.

510
00:47:03,403 --> 00:47:04,321
<i>Hideo.</i>

511
00:47:09,868 --> 00:47:11,245
Do you have anything else to say?

512
00:47:14,581 --> 00:47:16,166
No, Father.

513
00:47:33,767 --> 00:47:35,310
So-ran.

514
00:47:41,358 --> 00:47:42,234
Give it to me.

515
00:47:48,782 --> 00:47:50,033
I'll clean up the house.

516
00:47:50,117 --> 00:47:52,369
Forget everything for today
and get some rest.

517
00:47:53,120 --> 00:47:54,162
No.

518
00:47:54,997 --> 00:48:00,043
I need to keep myself busy
to forget all these thoughts for a while.

519
00:48:13,348 --> 00:48:14,725
About Seo-hee.

520
00:48:18,228 --> 00:48:20,355
The name I called her.

521
00:48:22,399 --> 00:48:23,317
Keum Seo-hee.

522
00:48:28,363 --> 00:48:29,406
Seo-hee…

523
00:48:31,658 --> 00:48:33,702
was my daughter's name.

524
00:48:38,415 --> 00:48:40,292
March 1st, 1919.

525
00:48:43,337 --> 00:48:45,380
<i>Not long after the March 1st Movement,</i>

526
00:48:46,089 --> 00:48:50,344
<i>I heard the Japanese</i>
<i>were burning villages in retaliation.</i>

527
00:48:52,012 --> 00:48:55,182
<i>But I didn't think our village</i>
<i>would be one of them.</i>

528
00:48:55,974 --> 00:48:56,892
<i>And then…</i>

529
00:48:57,559 --> 00:48:58,769
What's going on?

530
00:48:59,519 --> 00:49:01,730
No. Please, no. No!

531
00:49:02,564 --> 00:49:03,398
No!

532
00:49:03,482 --> 00:49:05,609
Please, no! Don't!

533
00:49:08,195 --> 00:49:09,404
It's okay, sweetie.

534
00:49:11,907 --> 00:49:13,909
Honey.

535
00:49:14,910 --> 00:49:17,579
Seok-jung, what's going on?
Why are they doing this?

536
00:49:21,208 --> 00:49:23,251
My wife and daughter
have nothing to do with it.

537
00:49:24,211 --> 00:49:25,212
Please let them go.

538
00:49:25,837 --> 00:49:28,090
Yes, there must be some misunderstanding.

539
00:49:28,173 --> 00:49:31,134
My husband is just a schoolteacher.

540
00:49:31,218 --> 00:49:33,261
My family has nothing to do with it.

541
00:49:33,804 --> 00:49:34,930
Let them go now.

542
00:49:35,013 --> 00:49:36,473
Shut up!

543
00:49:58,495 --> 00:49:59,579
Let me ask you again.

544
00:50:00,622 --> 00:50:04,209
Tell me who joined you in leading
the March 1st protest in this village.

545
00:50:05,752 --> 00:50:06,753
Otherwise…

546
00:50:17,723 --> 00:50:18,932
I'll kill your daughter.

547
00:50:22,102 --> 00:50:23,020
It's the daughter.

548
00:50:23,603 --> 00:50:24,646
No.

549
00:50:24,730 --> 00:50:25,772
No, please! Don't.

550
00:50:29,735 --> 00:50:31,028
Please, don't.

551
00:50:31,111 --> 00:50:33,488
No! Kill me, not her.

552
00:50:33,572 --> 00:50:35,490
Not my daughter. Please.

553
00:50:35,574 --> 00:50:37,367
Please, I'm begging you.

554
00:50:37,451 --> 00:50:38,493
Seok-jung.

555
00:50:38,577 --> 00:50:41,538
Honey, tell them something, honey.

556
00:50:41,621 --> 00:50:42,748
Honey.

557
00:50:42,831 --> 00:50:45,333
How many times did I tell you?
I did it by myself.

558
00:50:45,417 --> 00:50:47,294
The protest in this village

559
00:50:48,920 --> 00:50:49,838
was all me.

560
00:50:50,797 --> 00:50:52,007
I planned it all myself.

561
00:50:52,090 --> 00:50:53,008
Tell me.

562
00:50:53,759 --> 00:50:54,843
Who's your accomplice?

563
00:50:54,926 --> 00:50:55,802
Honey…

564
00:50:56,553 --> 00:50:58,055
Seok-jung!

565
00:50:59,431 --> 00:51:01,391
I swear, I did it alone.

566
00:51:12,861 --> 00:51:13,695
Shoot.

567
00:51:15,405 --> 00:51:16,490
No!

568
00:51:36,426 --> 00:51:37,385
Let go!

569
00:51:54,027 --> 00:51:56,113
This is your last chance.

570
00:51:56,196 --> 00:51:58,073
Tell me who else was involved.

571
00:51:58,615 --> 00:51:59,783
This time,

572
00:52:00,617 --> 00:52:01,451
it's your wife.

573
00:52:06,289 --> 00:52:07,332
I'm sorry.

574
00:52:12,462 --> 00:52:13,755
Na Byeong-sun,

575
00:52:16,216 --> 00:52:17,634
Choi Man-chun,

576
00:52:19,010 --> 00:52:20,720
and Kim Pung-san.

577
00:52:24,808 --> 00:52:26,101
Only three?

578
00:52:27,644 --> 00:52:28,562
Yes.

579
00:52:29,896 --> 00:52:31,273
Now, keep your word…

580
00:52:31,356 --> 00:52:32,440
Set it on fire.

581
00:52:32,524 --> 00:52:33,692
Set it on fire!

582
00:52:55,046 --> 00:52:56,339
No!

583
00:52:57,591 --> 00:52:59,342
This isn't what you promised.

584
00:53:00,427 --> 00:53:02,929
Those people are all innocent.

585
00:53:03,513 --> 00:53:06,224
Please, please, put out the fire.

586
00:53:06,808 --> 00:53:07,767
Please.

587
00:53:12,355 --> 00:53:15,775
I don't think I said I'd spare them.

588
00:53:25,035 --> 00:53:27,662
You damn monster!

589
00:53:28,538 --> 00:53:30,498
What did we ever do to deserve this?

590
00:53:32,334 --> 00:53:34,920
We only asked for our country back.

591
00:53:35,003 --> 00:53:37,589
We only cried out for independence!

592
00:53:38,256 --> 00:53:39,758
But you people…

593
00:53:39,841 --> 00:53:41,092
Take him away!

594
00:53:41,593 --> 00:53:44,012
You worthless bastards!

595
00:54:14,626 --> 00:54:16,586
No!

596
00:55:39,294 --> 00:55:41,838
<i>We had our daughter</i>
<i>after ten years of marriage,</i>

597
00:55:42,881 --> 00:55:44,549
<i>and that's how I lost her.</i>

598
00:55:48,470 --> 00:55:51,014
<i>I never went to school.</i>
<i>I couldn't even read or write.</i>

599
00:55:51,097 --> 00:55:53,433
<i>My husband and daughter were all I had.</i>

600
00:55:53,516 --> 00:55:55,393
<i>I was just a country woman,</i>

601
00:55:56,811 --> 00:55:58,188
<i>but that day</i>

602
00:55:59,022 --> 00:56:01,024
<i>completely changed my life.</i>

603
00:57:07,006 --> 00:57:07,924
<i>I'd once heard</i>

604
00:57:08,883 --> 00:57:12,804
<i>there was a place</i>
<i>called Gugukdan in Shanghai.</i>

605
00:57:14,472 --> 00:57:17,183
<i>So I made my way there,</i>
<i>risking my life time and again,</i>

606
00:57:17,267 --> 00:57:20,270
<i>crossing mountains, fields, and rivers.</i>

607
00:57:34,701 --> 00:57:36,828
A LIBERATED HOMELAND

608
00:57:43,001 --> 00:57:44,502
INDEPENDENCE FOR KOREA

609
00:57:54,220 --> 00:57:55,221
I want to kill…

610
00:58:00,268 --> 00:58:02,395
that bastard.

611
00:58:20,079 --> 00:58:22,165
<i>I learned how to fire a gun.</i>

612
00:58:22,248 --> 00:58:23,458
<i>I was determined</i>

613
00:58:23,541 --> 00:58:26,002
<i>to be the one to kill him</i>
<i>with my own hands.</i>

614
00:59:02,497 --> 00:59:03,414
This way.

615
00:59:30,024 --> 00:59:33,361
<i>I never imagined</i>
<i>it'd take this long to find him</i>

616
00:59:33,903 --> 00:59:36,823
<i>after he returned to Japan.</i>

617
00:59:38,575 --> 00:59:40,994
<i>When I heard he was coming back to Joseon,</i>

618
00:59:42,745 --> 00:59:44,872
<i>I cried until I had no tears left.</i>

619
00:59:47,542 --> 00:59:49,294
<i>Finally, my chance had come.</i>

620
00:59:50,295 --> 00:59:51,337
<i>But then…</i>

621
00:59:53,047 --> 00:59:56,509
<i>For 13 years,</i>
<i>I didn't know if he was alive or dead.</i>

622
00:59:56,593 --> 01:00:00,430
<i>The man I'd sworn to kill</i>
<i>if we ever crossed paths again.</i>

623
01:00:01,806 --> 01:00:02,890
<i>It was my husband.</i>

624
01:00:04,851 --> 01:00:08,688
<i>In that moment,</i>
<i>when I had to call her something…</i>

625
01:00:08,771 --> 01:00:09,814
Keum Seo-hee!

626
01:00:11,733 --> 01:00:15,486
<i>I called her Seo-hee.</i>

627
01:00:23,202 --> 01:00:25,163
For 13 years,

628
01:00:25,246 --> 01:00:28,916
I'd never spoken that name aloud.

629
01:00:33,921 --> 01:00:34,964
Seo-hee.

630
01:00:37,342 --> 01:00:39,886
I'd said that name
thousands of times a day.

631
01:00:41,929 --> 01:00:43,973
I suppose it just came out.

632
01:00:54,859 --> 01:00:56,486
In Shanghai,

633
01:00:58,696 --> 01:01:01,908
<i>every year on my daughter's birthday,</i>
<i>I managed to find seaweed</i>

634
01:01:02,408 --> 01:01:04,952
<i>and made a bowl of seaweed soup.</i>

635
01:01:11,793 --> 01:01:13,002
I don't think

636
01:01:15,296 --> 01:01:17,006
I could ever eat that.

637
01:01:56,003 --> 01:01:57,505
You didn't have to bring this.

638
01:01:58,423 --> 01:02:00,425
I hope your wife recovers well.

639
01:02:01,759 --> 01:02:03,636
I was deeply sorry to hear the news.

640
01:02:03,720 --> 01:02:05,096
My father also asked me to offer

641
01:02:05,596 --> 01:02:07,974
his deepest sympathy and condolences.

642
01:02:08,558 --> 01:02:09,809
Thank you.

643
01:02:12,228 --> 01:02:14,397
My wife is asleep
after taking some medicine.

644
01:02:20,111 --> 01:02:22,321
Sorry things are a little messy.

645
01:02:22,905 --> 01:02:24,991
I hope you'll understand.

646
01:02:25,074 --> 01:02:26,492
We only just got back.

647
01:02:29,495 --> 01:02:30,913
Last night must've been shocking.

648
01:02:32,206 --> 01:02:34,041
I'm sure you were both shaken.

649
01:02:36,043 --> 01:02:38,755
As I promised,
I didn't run a story about last night.

650
01:02:39,839 --> 01:02:40,715
Thank you.

651
01:02:47,472 --> 01:02:49,390
Is your maid all right?

652
01:02:51,642 --> 01:02:52,685
The maid…

653
01:02:52,769 --> 01:02:53,603
Oh, you mean Seo-hee?

654
01:02:54,854 --> 01:02:56,022
Yes.

655
01:02:56,105 --> 01:02:57,648
It seems like she's not here.

656
01:02:57,732 --> 01:02:59,567
Did she go out on an errand?

657
01:03:00,401 --> 01:03:02,820
I'm afraid she quit.

658
01:03:04,739 --> 01:03:05,573
She quit?

659
01:03:05,656 --> 01:03:07,867
I think she was shaken
by what happened yesterday.

660
01:03:09,285 --> 01:03:11,370
She's never seen a gun or blood before.

661
01:03:11,454 --> 01:03:13,790
I tried to convince her,
but she wouldn't change her mind.

662
01:03:15,958 --> 01:03:18,085
Yes, that's no surprise. I understand.

663
01:03:24,884 --> 01:03:26,677
Do you know where she lives?

664
01:03:27,804 --> 01:03:28,638
Her home?

665
01:03:29,722 --> 01:03:31,349
No, I don't. Why do you ask?

666
01:03:31,974 --> 01:03:35,311
If it weren't for her, something terrible
could've happened to my father.

667
01:03:35,895 --> 01:03:38,022
I wanted to thank her, at least.

668
01:03:39,440 --> 01:03:40,608
It's a shame she's gone.

669
01:03:42,568 --> 01:03:43,820
I appreciate the thought,

670
01:03:43,903 --> 01:03:46,322
but there's really no need
to go to such lengths.

671
01:03:47,198 --> 01:03:48,241
Very well.

672
01:03:55,998 --> 01:03:57,625
I'll see you later.

673
01:03:58,918 --> 01:04:00,002
Okay. Take care.

674
01:04:16,185 --> 01:04:17,770
They're looking for her.

675
01:04:21,065 --> 01:04:25,570
<i>If I had a million won</i>

676
01:04:26,153 --> 01:04:27,780
<i>I'd save up to go to America</i>

677
01:04:27,864 --> 01:04:29,824
We replaced the filling with cotton.

678
01:04:29,907 --> 01:04:31,993
It should be nice and fluffy.

679
01:04:32,869 --> 01:04:35,371
I'll ring the bell ten minutes
before your two hours are up.

680
01:04:35,454 --> 01:04:36,789
If you want to stay longer,

681
01:04:36,873 --> 01:04:39,500
just pull this cord on the wall.

682
01:04:40,710 --> 01:04:41,836
<i>And I'd buy…</i>

683
01:04:41,919 --> 01:04:43,379
Hang on. What time is it?

684
01:04:43,462 --> 01:04:44,297
Damn it.

685
01:04:44,380 --> 01:04:46,132
FIVE, FOUR, THREE, TWO, ONE

686
01:04:46,966 --> 01:04:48,593
They're always running over.

687
01:04:48,676 --> 01:04:49,635
Mister.

688
01:04:49,719 --> 01:04:52,221
You charge one won for a whole night.

689
01:04:52,305 --> 01:04:55,600
Isn't 50 jeon for two hours
during the day a bit much?

690
01:04:56,225 --> 01:04:58,185
You're really going to get rich.

691
01:04:58,269 --> 01:05:00,271
Now you realize that?

692
01:05:01,731 --> 01:05:03,232
That's why, Ga-kyung,

693
01:05:03,316 --> 01:05:06,611
if you marry me,
this pawnshop and inn will all be yours.

694
01:05:06,694 --> 01:05:08,946
Wasn't it your youngest's
100th day yesterday?

695
01:05:09,030 --> 01:05:10,364
Not yesterday. The day before.

696
01:05:10,448 --> 01:05:13,367
Hey, if you bring your boyfriend,

697
01:05:13,451 --> 01:05:15,494
I'll make it 30 jeon just for you.

698
01:05:15,578 --> 01:05:16,746
Come on.

699
01:05:16,829 --> 01:05:19,957
We've known each other for so long.
Can't you do better than 30?

700
01:05:20,041 --> 01:05:22,501
Other places are begging me
to come for free.

701
01:05:22,585 --> 01:05:24,962
What? Do you really have someone?

702
01:05:26,088 --> 01:05:27,340
It looks like you do.

703
01:05:27,423 --> 01:05:28,966
Hey, just bring him along.

704
01:05:29,050 --> 01:05:32,053
I'll let you stay the night for free,
not just during the day.

705
01:05:32,136 --> 01:05:33,846
You can't take that back.

706
01:05:34,805 --> 01:05:37,350
Just bring the guy here.

707
01:05:37,433 --> 01:05:40,269
Men know men.

708
01:05:41,562 --> 01:05:43,856
Here. This is for the bullets.

709
01:05:45,149 --> 01:05:47,026
All right.

710
01:05:48,444 --> 01:05:50,863
Just marry me, and all this will be yours.

711
01:05:50,947 --> 01:05:52,281
Thank you.

712
01:05:52,365 --> 01:05:55,159
If you find any more, bring them here,
not anywhere else.

713
01:05:55,242 --> 01:05:56,160
Okay.

714
01:05:58,037 --> 01:05:59,246
By the way,

715
01:05:59,330 --> 01:06:03,542
do people ever pawn something
and not come back for it for 13 years?

716
01:06:03,626 --> 01:06:06,253
Thirteen years? Who would do that?

717
01:06:06,837 --> 01:06:08,547
The interest alone after 13 years

718
01:06:08,631 --> 01:06:12,218
could buy that item back
several times over.

719
01:06:12,301 --> 01:06:13,552
Right?

720
01:06:13,636 --> 01:06:15,930
Unless the item meant a lot to them.

721
01:06:16,013 --> 01:06:19,892
If that's the case,
wouldn't they come back for it sooner?

722
01:06:20,518 --> 01:06:21,811
I mean

723
01:06:21,894 --> 01:06:25,481
something you wouldn't want anyone
to find at home--

724
01:06:25,564 --> 01:06:26,857
Welcome.

725
01:06:26,941 --> 01:06:28,609
- Welcome.
- Welcome.

726
01:06:29,235 --> 01:06:30,736
Excuse me.

727
01:06:30,820 --> 01:06:33,406
Have you been running this shop for long?

728
01:06:41,205 --> 01:06:42,164
Oh my.

729
01:06:43,124 --> 01:06:44,125
Hello.

730
01:06:46,919 --> 01:06:48,754
- Over there!
- Why? What?

731
01:07:09,525 --> 01:07:10,568
Got you.

732
01:07:11,152 --> 01:07:12,069
The pickpocket.

733
01:07:58,074 --> 01:08:01,994
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

734
01:08:02,912 --> 01:08:05,539
<i>Do you want to send another spy?</i>

735
01:08:05,623 --> 01:08:07,625
I said this is your last chance.

736
01:08:09,877 --> 01:08:12,797
Sin Tae-jin.
Does the inspector general know him?

737
01:08:12,880 --> 01:08:14,715
<i>I want to know all of a sudden.</i>

738
01:08:14,799 --> 01:08:16,550
<i>She's sharp and a good liar.</i>

739
01:08:16,634 --> 01:08:17,802
You look so gorgeous.

740
01:08:17,885 --> 01:08:20,471
<i>She's quick on her feet</i>
<i>and quick with her hands.</i>

741
01:08:20,554 --> 01:08:22,640
But she'll definitely put us in danger.

742
01:08:23,724 --> 01:08:25,434
<i>Do you want me to be a spy?</i>

743
01:08:25,518 --> 01:08:28,395
<i>You just do what we tell you.</i>

744
01:08:28,479 --> 01:08:30,147
I was wondering…

745
01:08:30,856 --> 01:08:33,150
<i>Why did you come</i>
<i>to the Government-General?</i>

746
01:08:39,073 --> 01:08:41,075
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
